win the World Cup final? (theconversation.com, 2026-07-17T02:59:08Z) - <p>A record 102 matches have been played, leaving just two games to decide the <a href=\"https://theconversation.com/topics/fifa-world-cup-2026-186405\">2026 FIFA World Cup</a>: the third-place playoff (between France and England) and the final. </p> <p>The championship match, <a href=\"https://www.sbs.com.au/ondemand/collection/fifa-world-cup-2026-live-and-upcoming\">to be played on Sunday evening US time</a>, will see Spain take on Argentina in a fitting finale between <a href=\"https://inside.fifa.com/fifa-world-ranking/men\">the worldâ€™s two highest-ranked teams</a>. </p> <p>So, how did each team reach the final â€“ and how may it play out?</p> <p></p> <h2>How we got here</h2> <p>Both sides en...","[3] World Cup VAR controversies show why human referees should decide where potential fouls begin (theconversation.com, 2026-07-16T21:22:02Z) - <p>Two contested decisions at the 2026 World Cup <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/sports/soccer/vargentina-reach-semi-finals-under-cloud-complaints-2026-07-13/\">have reignited debate</a> over how video assistant referee (VAR) reviews should work, and how far back a referee should look when deciding what counts as part of the same passage of play.</p> <p>VAR allows referees to review contentious incidents using replay footage, <a href=\"https://www.theifab.com/laws/latest/video-assistant-referee-var-protocol/\">with the human referee making the final decision</a>. Itâ€™s meant to catch â€œclear and obvious errorsâ€ or incidents that the on-field officials missed. A referee reviewing an incident m...","[4] What Cabo Verdeâ€™s World Cup debut means for African football (africasacountry.com, 2026-07-10T06:15:41.504236Z) - It happened. Cabo Verde lost to Argentina and exited the 2026 FIFA World Cup. And I couldnâ€™t be prouder. As a former football player, lifelong lover of the beautiful game, and Cabo Verdean-American, watching Cabo Verde compete on the world stage for the first time felt bigger than sports. What this team represented went far beyond the final score. At the start of the tournament, predictive models gave Cabo Verde almost no chance against former world champions Spain. The result: a stunning 0â€“0 draw anchored by seven saves from goalkeeper Josimar â€œVozinhaâ€ Dias. Against Uruguay, analysts dismissed Cabo Verdeâ€™s disciplined defensive strategy as no match for Marcelo Bielsaâ€™s aggressive attack..."],"accountableAttention":{"rule":"make-the-click-preserve-the-warrant","headlineMustPreserve":["attribution","modality","scope","uncertainty","correction state"],"forbiddenStrengthenings":["source claim to newsroom fact","may/could/alleged to does/did/proves","single case to trend","correlation to causation","reader demand to evidence"],"correctionSurfacePolicy":"Any later correction to a cited claim must be propagated to body copy, headline, social cards, feeds, JSON-LD, and syndicated packets."},"constraints":["This packet is research intake, not a publishable article.","sourceUrls are source material; candidateReferences are the CSL-shaped cited cut available to writing.","claims remain attributed and source-bound until a manuscript's editing and publishing gates settle them.","Attention surfaces may increase curiosity, but must not create factual commitments absent from the packet or manuscript references.","Publication still requires body citations, editing standards review, and an explicit publishing action."]}},{"kind":"koios.prior-research-context","assignmentId":"decolonization-geometry-football-cup-final-6a4684f5","warrant":"internal conceptual memory only; not current-event factual evidence","value":{"kind":"koios.prior-research-context-admission","at":"2026-07-19T15:04:03.000Z","assignmentId":"decolonization-geometry-football-cup-final-6a4684f5","terms":["geometry football cup final","decolonization","geometry","football","final"],"warrant":"internal conceptual memory only; no current-even